# AI Gateway route specificity

Envoy breaks equal header-match counts by keeping the **older** route. That flips after a Helm recreate. Do not rely on route age.

## Contract

When NeMo intercept is on:

- The unknown-model HTTPRoute matches **only** `x-zelkor-guardrails-bypass: 1` (Exact). It returns 400 `model_not_found`.
- Each provider bypass rule on `AIGatewayRoute` matches that bypass header **and** one `x-ai-eg-model` value. Two headers, so it beats the reject route.
- `x-ai-eg-model` values are a real provider regex or an Exact model id. Never `.+`, `.*`, `^.*$`, or `^.+$`.
- The no-match rule sends chat to NeMo. It is not a second reject route.

Same hostname + same header count as a provider rule is a tie. A catch-all model match on the reject route makes configured models 400.

```yaml
# BAD — ties provider regex rules
headers:
  - type: Exact
    name: x-zelkor-guardrails-bypass
    value: "1"
  - type: RegularExpression
    name: x-ai-eg-model
    value: ".+"

# GOOD — reject is bypass only; provider rules add the model header
headers:
  - type: Exact
    name: x-zelkor-guardrails-bypass
    value: "1"
```

## Tests

`tests/test_helm_ai_gateway_providers.py`: `test_bypass_reject_stays_less_specific_across_providers` and `test_templates_do_not_pair_bypass_with_catchall_model`. Extend them when adding an HTTPRoute or AIGatewayRoute on the AI Gateway host.
